      'Turn-flow example: 1. Setup: prepare players, deck or tiles, and opening layout according to the variant. 2. Turn loop: each player performs one legal action (play, capture, build, bet, or pass/draw as applicable). 3. Resolution: each action updates control of tricks/cards/pot/layout. 4. End condition: when hand-ending criteria are met, scoring is computed and match state advances.',
      'Scoring example: Each hand is settled for money: the player who dominoes, or who has the lowest total pips in hand when play is blocked, wins the bets they placed against the banker. Win individual games by playing your last tile or, in a blocked game, by having the lowest pip total; settle stakes between each non-banker and the banker according to the agreed minimum and maximum bets..',
